{
  "title": "78: al-Nabaa النبإ",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nعَمَّ يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَۚ‏(1)\nA’MMA YATA-SAAA-ALOON.\nOf what ask they one another?\nعَنِ النَّبَاِ الْعَظِيْمِۙ‏(2)\nA’NIN NABA-IL A’ZEEMIL\nOf the Great News\nالَّذِىْ هُمْ فِيْهِ مُخْتَلِفُوْنَؕ‏(3)\nLAZEE HUM FEEHE MUKHTALEFOON.\nThat which they therein differ\nكَلَّا سَيَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nKALLAA SA-YA’LAMOONA.\nVerily! they shall soon come to know\nثُمَّ كَلَّا سَيَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(5)\nSUMMA KALLAA SAYA’LAMOON.\nVerily, Verily, they shall soon come to know\nاَلَمْ نَجْعَلِ الْاَرْضَ مِهٰدًا ۙ‏(6)\nALAM NAJ-A’LIL ARZA MEHAADANW.\nWhat! Made We not the earth a wide expanse?\nوَّالْجِبَالَ اَوْتَادًا ۙ‏(7)\nWAL JEBAALA AWTAADANW\nAnd the mountains as bolts?\nوَّخَلَقْنٰكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا ۙ‏(8)\nWA KHALAQNAAKUM AZWAAJANW.\nAnd We created you in pairs\nوَّجَعَلْنَا نَوْمَكُمْ سُبَاتًا ۙ‏(9)\nWA JA-A’LNAA NAWMAKUM SOBAATANW.\nAnd cause your sleep a rest\nوَّجَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ لِبَاسًا ۙ‏(10)\nWA JA-A’LNAL LAYLA LEBAASANW.\nAnd caused the night a covering\nوَّجَعَلْنَا النَّهَارَ مَعَاشًا‏(11)\nWA JA-A’LNAN NAHAARA MA-A’ASHANW.\nAnd caused the day for (your) seeking livelihood\nوَّبَنَيْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعًا شِدَادًا ۙ‏(12)\nWA BANAYNAA FAWQAKUM SAB-A’N SHEDAADANW.\nAnd We have erected above you the seven strong ones\nوَّ جَعَلْنَا سِرَاجًا وَّهَّاجًا ۙ‏(13)\nWA JA-A’LNAA SERAAJANW WAH-HAAJANW.\nAnd We made therein a lamp burning\nوَّاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ الْمُعْصِرٰتِ مَآءً ثَجَّاجًا ۙ‏(14)\nWA ANZALNAA MENAL MO’SERAATE MAAA-AN SAJJAAJAL.\nAnd send We down from the clouds water in torrents\nلِّنُخْرِجَ بِهٖ حَبًّا وَّنَبَاتًا ۙ‏(15)\nLE-NUKHREJA BEHI HABBANW WA NABAATANW\nThat We may bring forth by it, corn and herbs\nوَّجَنّٰتٍ اَلْفَافًا ؕ‏(16)\nWA JANNAATIN ALFAAFAA.\nAnd gardens of thick foliage\nاِنَّ يَوْمَ الْفَصْلِ كَانَ مِيْقَاتًا ۙ‏(17)\nINNA YAWMAL FASLE KAANA MEEQAATANY.\nVerily the Day of Decision is a time appointed\nيَّوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَتَاْتُوْنَ اَفْوَاجًا ۙ‏(18)\nYAWMA TUNFAKHO FIS SOORE FA-TAATOONA AFWAAJANW.\nThe Day when the Trumpet shall be blown, and ye shall come forth in (huge) groups\nوَّفُتِحَتِ السَّمَآءُ فَكَانَتْ اَبْوَابًا ۙ‏(19)\nWA FOTEHATIS SAMAAA-O FA KAANAT ABWAABANW.\nAnd (they will find) the heaven opened, full of portals\nوَّ سُيِّرَتِ الْجِبَالُ فَكَانَتْ سَرَابًا ؕ‏(20)\nWA SUYYERATIL JEBAALO FA KAANAT SARAABAA.\nAnd (they will find) the mountains set in motion, as if they are a mere vapour\nاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ كَانَتْ مِرْصَادًا ۙ‏(21)\nINNA JAHANNAMA KAANAT MIRSAADAL.\nVerily (they will find) the hell in waiting\nلِّلطّٰغِيْنَ مَاٰبًا ۙ‏(22)\nLIT-TAAGHEENA MA-AABAL.\n(Being) for the transgressors the destination\nلّٰبِثِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَحْقَابًا ۚ‏(23)\nLAABESEENA FEEHAA AHQAABAA.\nTo abide therein for ages\nلَا يَذُوْقُوْنَ فِيْهَا بَرْدًا وَّلَا شَرَابًا ۙ‏(24)\nLAA YAZOOQOONA FEEHAA BARDANW WA LAA SHARAABAA.\nThey shall taste not therein any coolness nor any drink\nاِلَّا حَمِيْمًا وَّغَسَّاقًا ۙ‏(25)\nILLAA HAMEEMANW WA GHASSAAQAA.\nSave boiling water and running pus\nجَزَآءً وِّفَاقًا ؕ‏(26)\nJA-ZAAA-ANW WEFAAQAA.\nA recompense fitting (their evils)!\nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ حِسَابًا ۙ‏(27)\nINNAHUM KAANOO LAA YARJOONA HESAABANW.\nVerily they looked not forward to their reckoning\nوَّكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا كِذَّابًا ؕ‏(28)\nWA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA KIZZAABAA.\nAnd belied Our Signs with a (persistent) falsification\nوَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ اَحْصَيْنٰهُ كِتٰبًا ۙ‏(29)\nWA KULLA SHAY-IN AHSAYNAAHO KETAABAA.\nAnd everything have We recorded in a book\nفَذُوْقُوْا فَلَنْ نَّزِيْدَكُمْ اِلَّا عَذَابًا‏(30)\nFA-ZOOQOO FALAN NAZEEDAKUM ILLAA A’ZAABAA.\nTaste ye then! And never will We increase for you aught but chastisement!\nاِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ مَفَازًا ۙ‏(31)\nINNA LIL MUTTAQEENA MAFAAZAA.\nVerily for the pious ones is a great realization.\nحَدَآئِقَ وَاَعْنَابًا ۙ‏(32)\nHADAAA-EQA WA A-A’NAABANW\nGardens enclosed and vineyards\nوَّكَوَاعِبَ اَتْرَابًا ۙ‏(33)\nWA KAWAA-E’BA ATRAABANW.\nAnd mates, maidens beautiful\nوَّكَاْسًا دِهَاقًا ؕ‏(34)\nWA KAASAN DEHAAQAA.\nAnd a cup full\nلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا لَغْوًا وَّلَا كِذّٰبًا ۚ‏(35)\nLAA YAS-MA-O’ONA FEEHAA LAGHWANW WA LAA KIZZAABAA.\nThey shall hear not therein vain words nor any falsehood\nجَزَآءً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ عَطَآءً حِسَابًا ۙ‏(36)\nJA-ZAAA-AM MIR RABBEKA A’TAAA-AN HESAABAR.\nA recompense from thy Lord, an award according to the reckoning\nرَّبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا الرَّحْمٰنِ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مِنْهُ خِطَابًا ۚ‏(37)\nRABBIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAR RAHMAANE LAA YAMLEKOONA MINHO KHETAABAA.\nThe Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them two, the Beneficent God, they shall possess not the right of addressing\nيَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الرُّوْحُ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ صَفًّا ؕۙ لَّا يَتَكَلَّمُوْنَ اِلَّا مَنْ اَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَقَالَ صَوَابًا‏(38)\nYAWMA YAQOOMUR ROOHO WAL MALAAA-EKATO SAFFAL, LAA YATAKALLAMOONA ILLAA MAN AZENA LAHUR RAHMAANO WA QAALA SAWAABAA.\nOn the day whereon shall stand the spirit and the angels arrayed, they shall speak not save he whom the Beneficent God giveth leave, who spoke (only) the truth\nذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمُ الْحَقُّ ۚ فَمَنْ شَآءَ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ مَاٰبًا‏(39)\nZAALEKAL YAWMUL HAQQ, FAMAN SHAAA-AT TAKHAZA ELAA RABBEHI MA-AABAA.\nThat is the day certain, whoso then desireth, may take refuge unto his Lord.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْذَرْنٰكُمْ عَذَابًا قَرِيْبًا ۖۚ  يَّوْمَ يَنْظُرُ الْمَرْءُ مَا قَدَّمَتْ يَدٰهُ وَيَقُوْلُ الْكٰفِرُ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ كُنْتُ تُرٰبًا‏(40)\nINNAA ANZARNAAKUM A’ZAABAN QAREEBAN-Y, YAWMA YANZORUL MAR-O MAA QADDAMAT YADAAHO WA YAQOOLUL KAAFERO YAA LAYTANEE KUNTO TORAABAA.\nVerily have We warned you of a chastisement nigh at hand, the day when man shall see what have sent before his two hands, and when the disbeliever shall say, ‘‘Oh! would that I were dust!",
  "merits": "There are 40 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah everyday will be fortunate enough to visit Masjidul Haraam in the same year. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that memorization of this Surah carries great reward.\nIf this Surah is recited with the intention of staying awake, then the reciter will not fall asleep and if it is recited before travelling then the journey will become easy. Drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved cures stomach problems."
